From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run the audio service in the browser process on Windows

Default AudioServiceOutOfProcess to disabled on Windows, so the audio
service runs in the browser process. Social Club replaces the browser's
--disable-features for its children, so the switch cannot do this; a
compiled default it never names can. One process, its threads and its
JIT pool copies fewer under Playport (decision 0111, PLA-381).
Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-cef-audio-in-process.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 content/public/common/content_features.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/public/common/content_features.cc b/content/public/common/content_features.cc
index d70d0da717..d74762ee02 100644
--- a/content/public/common/content_features.cc
+++ b/content/public/common/content_features.cc
@@ -105,8 +105,10 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kAttachUnownedInnerWebContents, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAudioServiceLaunchOnStartup, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Runs the audio service in a separate process.
+// Off on Windows: an embedder that must fit several processes in a small
+// address space runs it in the browser process.
 BASE_FEATURE(kAudioServiceOutOfProcess,
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT
 #else
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT
